---
import Alert from "@/components/Alert.astro";
import H from "@/components/H.astro";
import Layout from "@/layouts/PageLayout.astro";
import Section from "@/components/Section.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="FRC 12148"
    description="Team V.A.N. is a student-led FIRST Robotics Competition team in Palm Bay, Florida, serving students in southern Brevard and Indian River counties."
>
    <H class="mb-4">About Team V.A.N.</H>

    <p>
        Team V.A.N. (FRC 12148) is a student-led FIRST Robotics Competition team
        based in Palm Bay, serving students in southern Brevard County and
        Indian River County.
    </p>

    <Alert title="Student kickoff is November 2" class="mt-6">
        <p>
            Location:{" "}
            <a
                href="https://themindforgeguild.org"
                class="text-blue-300 underline underline-offset-4"
            >
                Mind Forge Guild
            </a>
        </p>
        <p>
            The team calendar is shared publicly.{" "}
            <a
                href="https://calendar.google.com/calendar/u/0?cid=ZnJjMTIxNDhAZ21haWwuY29t"
                class="text-blue-300 underline underline-offset-4"
            >
                <strong>click here</strong>
            </a>{" "}
            to add it to your own.
        </p>
    </Alert>

    <Section aria-labelledby="organization-heading">
        <H id="organization-heading" level="h2">
            How the team is organized
        </H>
        <p>
            Team V.A.N. is student-run, with adult mentors coaching rather than
            directing. Four team leads manage organization and business,
            ensuring the team runs smoothly and that responsibilities are
            clearly defined.
        </p>
        <p>
            Beyond that, membership is not divided into fixed subteams. Students
            are free to work wherever they're most interested or most useful
            that week, whether that's wiring one day and CAD the next, and
            nobody is locked into one group for the season. Team leads
            coordinate the work and mentors provide technical guidance and
            safety oversight, but day-to-day problem solving is student-driven.
        </p>
        <p>
            Experienced students train new members and keep notes on both the
            technical work and how the team is run, so responsibilities and
            institutional knowledge can be handed off to future leaders as the
            team grows.
        </p>
    </Section>

    <Section>
        <H level="h2">What we do</H>
        <p>
            Founded in 2026, Team V.A.N. (FRC 12148) is in its first FRC season.
            Students run the technical work and the day-to-day organization of
            the team, with four leads managing organization and business. Where
            we meet and build is on the{" "}
            <a
                href="/about/"
                class="text-blue-300 underline underline-offset-4"
            >
                What Is FIRST
            </a>{" "}
            page.
        </p>
        <p>
            Our main build space is in Palm Bay, near Palm Bay Magnet, Bayside
            High, and Heritage High. We are also the closest FRC team to
            Sebastian River High, Vero Beach High, and Indian River Charter
            High.
        </p>

        <H level="h2">Why this team exists</H>
        <p>
            We started the team because southern Brevard County and Indian River
            County have had limited access to FRC. Indian River County currently
            has no FRC teams, and students in southern Brevard often have to
            travel a long way to join an existing program.
        </p>

        <H level="h2">Who we serve</H>
        <p>
            Indian River County currently has no local FRC team, and students in
            southern Brevard often face transportation and financial barriers to
            existing programs. Palm Bay Magnet Senior High operates under a
            Title I schoolwide program, and Bayside High and Heritage High serve
            significant populations of economically disadvantaged students.
        </p>

        <H level="h2">This season</H>
        <p>
            We expect 15 to 20 committed members this season. We plan to compete
            at the Orlando Regional and the Rocket City Regional, and at the
            FIRST Championship if we qualify. Competition dates and venues are
            on the{" "}
            <a
                href="/competitions/"
                class="text-blue-300 underline underline-offset-4"
            >
                Competitions
            </a>{" "}
            page.
        </p>

        <H level="h2">Join us</H>
        <p>
            Students interested in building, programming or business are
            welcome. Anyone can join, regardless of experience.{" "}
            <a
                href="/interest/"
                class="text-blue-300 underline underline-offset-4"
            >
                Fill out the interest form
            </a>
            .
        </p>

        <H level="h2">Want to help?</H>
        <p>
            If you are in the area and would like to support the team, you can
            reach us at{" "}
            <a
                href="mailto:contact@teamvan.org"
                class="text-blue-300 underline underline-offset-4"
            >
                contact@teamvan.org
            </a>
            .
        </p>
    </Section>
</Layout>
